What are the charges?
With The People's Pension, you pay an annual management charge made up of 3 elements - an annual charge, an ongoing
management charge of 0.5% (50p for every £100 saved) and a rebate on the management charge. The rebate level depends on how much is in your pension pot. When you take money out, we'll work out future rebates on the value of your remaining savings.
For more information, visit www.thepeoplespension.co.uk/charge
To find out exactly how much you're charged, please log into your Online Account at
www.thepeoplespension.co.uk/viewaccount and go to 'Manage my pension', followed by 'Charges'.
Keep track of your pension
You can view all your pension information at any time using your Online Account. Your annual statement, showing how your
pension is doing, will be sent and stored here too. Log on or register at: https://myproducts.peoplespartnership.co.uk/
How much will the advice cost?
We can't advise you on the suitability of this product; therefore there will be no charge for advice. You may wish to seek financial
advice from an authorised adviser, who may charge you for this service. You can find an adviser by visiting www.unbiased.co.uk which will help you locate one in your area.

